From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:11:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 192/192] wifi: ath11k: offer beacon protection only where the
 firmware signs beacons

Advertise beacon protection only with firmware of the WLAN.HK.2.12 line
or newer. Checked on air with a BE200 sniffer against the BIGTK the
client received, MIC computed as 802.11-2024 12.5.3.5 and wlantest do:
QCN9074 WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146 and IPQ5018 WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1-01744 send the
MME with the right key ID and an increasing BIPN but a MIC that verifies
under no key and no masking variant, so clients enforcing beacon
protection drop every beacon; QCN9074 WLAN.HK.2.12-01460 and
WLAN.HK.2.13-01309 MICs verify, and a BE200 enforcing it stays
connected.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index 3b4b569..63f8b2d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -11461,8 +11461,13 @@ static int __ath11k_mac_register(struct ath11k *ar)
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy,
 				      NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_ENABLE_FTM_RESPONDER);
 
+	/* Firmware before the WLAN.HK.2.12 line (the top byte of fw_version:
+	 * 0x27 for 2.7, 0x29 for 2.9, 0x2c for 2.12) advertises the service but
+	 * puts a MIC in the beacons that does not verify.
+	 */
 	if (test_bit(WMI_TLV_SERVICE_BEACON_PROTECTION_SUPPORT, ar->ab->wmi_ab.svc_map) &&
-	    !test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_HW_CRYPTO_DISABLED, &ab->dev_flags))
+	    !test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_HW_CRYPTO_DISABLED, &ab->dev_flags) &&
+	    ab->qmi.target.fw_version >> 24 >= 0x2c)
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy,
 				      NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_BEACON_PROTECTION);
 
